tation]\n    E003 --> E005\n    E004 --> E005\n    E001 --> E005\n```\n\n## DAG Justification\n\n| Edge | Rule | Rationale |\n|------|------|-----------|\n| E001 → E002 | Rule 12/13 (framework → consumer) | The gallery's launch code builds against the tutorial package format (reads tutorial metadata, pinned images, artifact locations to spawn a workbench or import a pipeline). The format is a build-against artifact, not a configuration reference. |\n| E001 → E003 | Rule 12/13 (framework → consumer) | Authored tutorials are delivered as packages conforming to the format (metadata, pinned images, validation manifest) so they are versioned and testable; the packaging format must exist before the tutorial deliverables are produced against it. |\n| E001 → E004 | Rule 12/13 (framework → consumer) | Same as above — the pipeline tutorial is delivered as a package conforming to the format. |\n| E001 → E005 | Rule 11 (docs last) | docs-authoring epic is blocked by ALL Implementation epics in the strategy. |\n| E002 → E005 | Rule 11 (docs last) | Documentation describes what was built, including the gallery. |\n| E003 → E005 | Rule 11 (docs last) | Documentation covers the tutorial set and contribution process. |\n| E004 → E005 | Rule 11 (docs last) | Documentation covers the tutorial set and contribution process. |\n\nNo edges between E002, E003, and E004: once the format exists, the Dashboard\ngallery, the notebook tutorials, and the pipeline tutorial are work in different\ncomponents/repos with no shared build artifacts — they run in parallel (Rules\n14/15). The gallery is verified against packaged tutorials via an acceptance\ncriterion, not a DAG edge.\n\n## HLR Traceability Matrix\n\n| HLR | Priority | Epic(s) |\n|-----|----------|---------|\n| HLR-1 | P0 | E002 — Dashboard tutorial gallery with one-click launch |\n| HLR-2 | P0 | E003 (five notebook tutorials: first workbench, data prep, first training run, first deployment, first RAG app) and E004 (first pipeline tutorial) — split by component/team boundary (Notebooks/Workbenches vs Data Science Pipelines/RHOAI Pipelines), not by priority |\n| HLR-3 | P1 | E001 — epic priority elevated to P0 by priority inheritance: the format gates all P0 work (HLR-1 gallery and HLR-2 tutorials all build against it) |\n| HLR-4 | P2 | E005 — docs-authoring epic; priority derived from strategy frontmatter `priority: Major` → P1 per the docs-authoring priority exception (not P2, and it does not push priority upstream) |\n\nAll four HLRs are covered; no orphaned requirements. HLR-2's split across E003\nand E004 follows the epic boundary rule (different component OR different team →\nseparate epics): the pipeline tutorial is a different artifact type (KFP v2\npipeline vs notebook) owned by a different team.\n\n## Health Warnings\n\n1. **Missing strategy sections**: the strategy has no Impacted Teams table, no\n   Dependencies table, no Given/When/Then acceptance criteria, and no\n   Non-Functional Requirements; Affected Components is a bullet list without\n   owner teams or change descriptions. Owner teams were inferred from\n   `.context/architecture-context/` (Dashboard → RHOAI Dashboard, Notebooks →\n   Workbenches, Data Science Pipelines → RHOAI Pipelines).\n2. **Documentation team assumed**: no Impacted Teams table exists and the\n   Documentation component has no architecture-context file, so the owning team\n   for E005 is assumed to be \"RHOAI Documentation\" — verify before scheduling.\n3. **Epic size — E003 over the ~2-week guideline**: E003 authors and tests five\n   notebook tutorials; at roughly 2–4 days of authoring plus release-testing per\n   tutorial that is ~2–3 sprints of effort. Kept whole because the five\n   tutorials are one logical change (one curated, tested content set for the\n   same component, team, packaging format, and review process) and a split\n   would duplicate the packaging/validation and review setup across fragments\n   with no independent user value per fragment. Re-split trigger: if authored\n   tutorial content exceeds ~3 sprints of effort, or any single tutorial's\n   authoring-plus-testing exceeds one sprint, split E003 into two content epics\n   along the journey list (e.g. workbench/data-prep/training vs\n   deployment/RAG).\n4. **Priority note (not an inversion)**: HLR-3 is labeled P1 in the strategy,\n   but its epic (E001) is P0 by priority inheritance because every P0\n   deliverable (gallery and tutorials) builds against the packaging format.\n   If the strategy author intended the format to be deferrable, the P0 work\n   would need to proceed against an ad-hoc metadata convention — flag for\n   confirmation in refinement.\n5. **Documentation component has no architecture-context file**: Documentation\n   is a content component, not a platform software component, so no\n   repo-onboarding/konflux-onboarding chain was generated for it; E005 is a\n   docs-authoring epic only.\n\n## Tiered Delivery\n\nNot applicable — the strategy has no external dependencies with uncertain\ntiming; all work is internal to the platform's components and teams.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":31095,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bbadf3c5aa7216ec","agent_id":"ab3b8d69a816e456b","session_id":"6bb350ac-77bc-4e4b-90d8-d4ea0771fd78","uuid":"f8f4dcf8-cdb3-467e-b28d-d592b359098e","timestamp":"2026-10-26T20:36:04.088Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9019"}
