{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-9db76e6f-0565-4cb9-9a3a-6b0aa04af0fd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-b6a378c8732113f7","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9019-1i8g_nn_/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9019-E001.md","content":"# Tutorial packaging format (metadata, pinned images, validation manifest)\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic defines the tutorial packaging format that makes tutorials versioned\nand testable independently of Dashboard releases: the metadata a packaged\ntutorial carries, the pinned workbench images it references, and the validation\nmanifest used to test it against a release. The format is the contract between\nthe tutorial gallery (which launches packaged tutorials) and tutorial authors\n(who produce them), so it is defined before either the gallery or the tutorials\nare built.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Define the tutorial package format covering, per the strategy: metadata,\n  pinned images, and a validation manifest.\n- Specify how a package is versioned so tutorials can be updated and tested on\n  their own cadence, decoupled from Dashboard releases.\n- Specify how the validation manifest is used to test a tutorial against a\n  given release (the mechanism the curated tutorial set is tested with).\n- Cover both tutorial kinds the gallery launches: a notebook launched into a\n  workbench, and a pipeline imported into a project.\n- Keep the format a contract only — the gallery implementation and the tutorial\n  content are separate work.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- The packaging format is documented and covers metadata, pinned images, and a\n  validation manifest for both notebook-based and pipeline-based tutorials.\n- A tutorial package can be versioned, and its version is distinguishable from\n  the Dashboard release it is tested against.\n- Given a packaged tutorial and a target release, the validation manifest\n  defines a runnable pass/fail test of the tutorial against that release, and\n  this is demonstrated on at least one sample package of each kind (notebook\n  and pipeline).\n- The format is reviewed with the teams that consume it (the Dashboard gallery\n  implementers and the tutorial authors) and their feedback is incorporated.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-3 (P1) — \"A tutorial packaging format (metadata, pinned images,\n  validation manifest) is defined so tutorials are versioned and testable\n  independently of Dashboard releases.\" This epic fully covers HLR-3. Epic\n  priority is P0 by inheritance: every P0 deliverable of the strategy (the\n  gallery and the curated tutorials) builds against this format.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":33374,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bbadf3c5aa7216ec","agent_id":"ab3b8d69a816e456b","session_id":"6bb350ac-77bc-4e4b-90d8-d4ea0771fd78","uuid":"40ae5d18-293f-4c4e-a9bf-14055a3b506e","timestamp":"2026-10-26T20:36:18.253Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9019"}
