{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-6e28fa2c-60ad-45db-83fb-f2923052e411","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-8bf87ddbf9f2d8cf","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9019-1i8g_nn_/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9019-E002.md","content":"# Dashboard tutorial gallery with one-click launch into a project\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic delivers the tutorial gallery in the Dashboard: a curated, visible\ngallery of getting-started tutorials from which a user can launch a tutorial\ninto their own project with one click — opening a workbench preloaded with the\ntutorial notebook, or importing the tutorial pipeline into the project. This is\nthe product-code work stream of the strategy, owned by the Dashboard team.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Add a tutorial gallery surface to the Dashboard (listing curated tutorials\n  with their metadata from the tutorial packaging format).\n- Implement one-click launch into the user's project:\n  - For notebook tutorials: spawn a workbench with the tutorial notebook,\n    using the pinned image from the tutorial package.\n  - For pipeline tutorials: import the pipeline into the user's project.\n- Launch mechanics operate through the existing Kubernetes CR surfaces the\n  Dashboard already reads and writes (Notebook CRs, pipeline resources).\n- Gallery visibility/enablement follows the Dashboard's existing per-component\n  feature flag mechanism.\n- Incidental UI text and screenshot updates that fall out of this change are\n  included here; no new documentation topics are authored in this epic.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given a user with a project, when they open the tutorial gallery and click a\n  notebook tutorial, then a workbench opens in their project running the\n  tutorial notebook on the pinned image.\n- Given a user with a project, when they click a pipeline tutorial, then the\n  tutorial pipeline is imported 