{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a31c95eaabee0f04","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9019-E001\n3\ttitle: Tutorial packaging format (metadata, pinned images, validation manifest)\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9019\n5\tcomponent: Notebooks\n6\tteam: Workbenches\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 0\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n14\t  existing_foundation: -1\n15\t  open_questions: 1\n16\t  external_dependency: 1\n17\t  human_process_gates: 0\n18\t  repo_access: 1\n19\t  architecture_claims: 1\n20\timplementation_type: null\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 3\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Tutorial packaging format (metadata, pinned images, validation manifest)\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tThis epic defines the tutorial packaging format that makes tutorials versioned\n34\tand testable independently of Dashboard releases: the metadata a packaged\n35\ttutorial carries, the pinned workbench images it references, and the validation\n36\tmanifest used to test it against a release. The format is the contract between\n37\tthe tutorial gallery (which launches packaged tutorials) and tutorial authors\n38\t(who produce them), so it is defined before either the gallery or the tutorials\n39\tare built.\n40\t\n41\t## Scope\n42\t\n43\t- Define the tutorial package format covering, per the strategy: metadata,\n44\t  pinned images, and a validation manifest.\n45\t- Specify how a package is versioned so tutorials can be updated and tested on\n46\t  their own cadence, decoupled from Dashboard releases.\n47\t- Specify how the validation manifest is used to test a tutorial against a\n48\t  given release (the mechanism the curated tutorial set is tested with).\n49\t- Cover both tutorial kinds the gallery launches: a notebook launched into a\n50\t  workbench, and a pipeline imported into a project.\n51\t- Keep the format a contract only — the gallery implementation and the tutorial\n52\t  content are separate work.\n53\t\n54\t## Acceptance Criteria\n55\t\n56\t- The packaging format is documented and covers metadata, pinned images, and a\n57\t  validation manifest for both notebook-based and pipeline-based tutorials.\n58\t- A tutorial package can be versioned, and its version is distinguishable from\n59\t  the Dashboard release it is tested against.\n60\t- Given a packaged tutorial and a target release, the validation manifest\n61\t  defines a runnable pass/fail test of the tutorial against that release, and\n62\t  this is demonstrated on at least one sample package of each kind (notebook\n63\t  and pipeline).\n64\t- The format is reviewed with the teams that consume it (the Dashboard gallery\n65\t  implementers and the tutorial authors) and their feedback is incorporated.\n66\t\n67\t## HLR Traceability\n68\t\n69\t- HLR-3 (P1) — \"A tutorial packaging format (metadata, pinned images,\n70\t  validation manifest) is defined so tutorials are versioned and testable\n71\t  independently of Dashboard releases.\" This epic fully covers HLR-3. Epic\n72\t  priority is P0 by inheritance: every P0 deliverable of the strategy (the\n73\t  gallery and the curated tutorials) builds against this format.\n74\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b4498af45c591be3","agent_id":"a45da96e282cf5d9d","session_id":"6bb350ac-77bc-4e4b-90d8-d4ea0771fd78","uuid":"3e052f15-ee1e-4699-b6eb-1ee55e9ff146","timestamp":"2026-10-26T20:44:49.240Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a31c95eaabee0f04","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9019"}
